## 🔬 Research Methodology & Analytical Approach

This engagement followed a structured consulting methodology across five phases:

**1. Market Intelligence Gathering**
- Emaar South area profiling: masterplan, infrastructure, connectivity, lifestyle
- Al Maktoum International Airport expansion analysis (DAEP official data)
- Expo City Dubai economic legacy assessment (EY 2023 economic impact study)

**2. Project-Level Due Diligence**
- Unit mix, sizing, entry pricing, handover timelines (Emaar official + Property Finder)
- Amenity benchmarking across both projects
- Payment plan structure analysis (10/70/20 construction-linked)

**3. Market Pricing Validation**
- Price-per-sq.ft benchmarking vs. Dubai citywide average (DLD/Engel & Völkers)
- Community-level PSF growth analysis (+19.3%–22.8% YoY, two independent sources)
- Historical pricing trend analysis (2023–2026 launch prices)

**4. DLD Transaction Validation**
- 50 verified Golf Acres pre-registration sale transactions (DLD Open Data via Propsearch.ae)
- PSF range: AED 1,295–1,777/sq.ft across 1-bed and 3-bed units
- Greenspoint: no comparable public transaction footprint located (flagged as a liquidity gap)

**5. Risk-Adjusted Scoring**
- Six-dimension weighted scorecard (Budget Fit 30%, Developer 15%, Liquidity 15%, Connectivity 10%, Livability 10%, Regulatory Risk 10%, Appreciation Exposure 10%)
- Traffic-light risk matrix across 8 risk categories
- Competitor benchmarking against Dubai Hills Estate, Creek Harbour, and The Valley

